#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#In this example, the engine and any rigid parts which move together with the engine such as the transmission, clutch/torque converter, etc. are treated as one independently sprung rigid body, separate from the vehicle sprung mass.
#
#The engine is mounted transversely in the front of the vehicle and is suspended by two mounts. Engine body roll rotation is controlled by a torque rod.
#
#The vehicle is performing an acceleration and braking test on a constant diameter circle road, allowing you to view the engine mount forces as the transmission shifts.
#
#Engine body location and engine mount properties are specified on the "Engine Mounts: Engine Mass and Geometry" screen. This screen is linked to the Vehicle: Sprung Mass screen. Browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen and click on the Sprung Mass blue link. Once on the Sprung Mass screen, click the blue link for the Engine Mount.
#
#A CarSim Engine Mount license is required to run the math model for this example. However, you can still view the simulation results provided with CarSim by clicking the "Video" and "Plot" buttons.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

